# rule.always.file-an-incident-for-a-defect-you-name-in-yourself

> **a defect you name in your own conduct is a claim against yourself. record it the same turn, before the reply that names it.**

applies the basis: an ack in prose trusts a memory that compaction erases; land the defect where the next self reads it.
counts: an ack of a correction ("you are right", "I should have", "my mistake", "I missed") · a miss you find alone, the same.
the record: the fix itself, when safe, clean, and landed this turn (cite its sha) · else a learner brief (the lesson) or a caught dream (the fix owed); the reply cites it.
test: **did the defect I just named land as a record, or only as prose?**
blocker: an admitted defect of your own with no record in the same turn
